  "mechanism_analysis": {
    "candidate_mechanism": "ACTIVE-EVIDENCE-INDUCED OVERCOMMITMENT (candidate, not proven): under G3-B.3 the active Strict tools return a coherent set of POSITIVE-LOOKING but non-decisive signals (authentic linkage, fresh restage, complete coverage, symptom non-reproduction). GPT appears to convert that affirmative diagnostic bundle into failure-free acceptability, whereas the silent static T2D surface gives no such positive evidence and always yields abstention.",
    "observation_active_Strict_DeepSeek": [
      "DeepSeek Strict abstains 10/10 in both gates. In G3-B.3 it actively queried the tools (and fetched the tier-D artifact in 8/10 cells, seeing the all-PASSED pre-patch baseline map) yet still abstained — active querying alone did not move it."
    ],
    "observation_active_Strict_GPT": [
      "GPT Strict abstained 10/10 in G3-B but committed ACCEPT on 7/10 in G3-B.3 (the other 3 still abstain). All 7 committed cells did NOT fetch the artifact; they committed from the linkage=true + fresh=true + coverage-complete + symptom-gone tool sequence (see g3b4_gpt_strict_audit)."
    ],
    "observation_static_T2D": [
      "T2D-T serves a static tier-D surface with NO tools and NO freshness signal. Both models abstain NEED_EVIDENCE on all 10/10 issues in BOTH G3-B and G3-B.3 — static restricted evidence never licenses a commitment for either model."
    ],
    "supporting_pattern": "The within-G3-B.3 contrast is suggestive: T2D (no tools) 10/10 abstain for both models; DeepSeek (uses tools, high scepticism) 10/10 abstain; GPT (uses tools) 3/10 abstain. Activeness is associated with movement only for the less sceptical model, consistent with — but not demonstrating — the candidate mechanism.",
    "why_not_causally_identified": [
      "This is a cross-version, ASSOCIATIONAL contrast. Between G3-B and G3-B.3 more than activeness changed: the G3-B structural freshness defect served fresh_state=FALSE, while G3-B.3 serves fresh_state=TRUE, and the Coverage/trust rules were corrected at the same time.",
      "Therefore the 10/10 -> 3/10 GPT Strict abstention shift cannot be attributed to active querying separately from the freshness/trust repair. A design that holds freshness and trust fixed while toggling only tool availability is needed (proposed for Gate 3-C, not executed)."
    ]
  },
